# `qa/live-results/` used to be ignored, back when it held throwaway screenshots
# from the browser harness. It now holds the Phase 7 evidence: fifteen images
# that cost real money, cannot be regenerated for free, and are the only way to
# check the claims in qa/live-results/README.md. Ignoring that is ignoring the
# deliverable. Outputs and prompts are committed; nothing here is read at build
# time, and no input images are copied in — the fixtures already ship in
# public/examples/ and report.json names the one each run used.
